  "paragraph": 7,
  "text": "To see why that explodes your bill, zoom inside an AI GPU like an H100. Massive high-bandwidth memory, or HBM, stores the model weights, linked by a narrow memory bus to ultra-fast on-chip SRAM and Tensor Cores. Those math units pack around a thousand teraflops of compute, but every byte must cross that bandwidth pipe first.",
